  "question": {
    "text": "The spin only magnetic moment ( $\\mu$ ) value (B.M.) of the compound with strongest oxidising power among $\\mathrm{Mn}_2 \\mathrm{O}_3, \\mathrm{TiO}$ and VO is ____ B.M. (Nearest integer).",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Strongest oxidising power among the option is $\\mathrm{Mn}_2 \\mathrm{O}_3$ because of $\\mathrm{E}^{\\circ}$ value\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{E}_{\\mathrm{Mn}^{+3} / \\mathrm{Mn}^{+2}}^{\\circ}=+1.57 \\mathrm{~V} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{Mn}^{+3} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{~d}^4 \\text { configuration } \\\\\n& \\mu=\\sqrt{24} \\mathrm{BM} \\\\\n& =4.89 \\mathrm{BM} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow 5\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
